## Pin graph object FQNs to the loaded domain version
================================================================================

Context:
Knowledge Graph Overview in the deployed app queried
``triplestore_bigcustomers100m_V2_graph`` while the user had loaded V1
(only V1 UC objects exist). Load posted JSON ``version: 1`` (int); document
keys are strings, so ``1 in versions`` missed and ``import_from_file``
silently selected lexicographic latest (``"2"``).

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/domain/payload.py
   ``select_loaded_version`` / ``loaded_version_document``: stringify the
   requested version, pin to it even if that slice is missing, and pick
   numeric latest only when no version was requested.
2. src/back/objects/session/DomainSession.py
   Versioned import uses ``loaded_version_document`` instead of
   ``version in versions`` + lexicographic ``sorted(..., reverse=True)``.
3. src/back/core/helpers/SQLHelpers.py
   ``effective_view_table`` / ``effective_graph_name`` stringify
   ``current_version`` so FQNs stay ``…_V1`` when the session version is int 1.
4. src/back/objects/domain/__init__.py
   Export ``select_loaded_version``.
5. tests/units/domain/test_payload_version_select.py
   New. Int vs string keys, numeric latest, missing-slice pin.
6. tests/units/domain/test_domain_session.py
   Import of V1 with ``version=1`` keeps ontology and ``delta.table_name``
   on V1.
7. tests/units/core/test_uri_sql_helpers.py
   Integer ``current_version`` still yields ``…_V1``.

