## Stop Overview and the KG status badge from scanning pass-through graph views
================================================================================

Context:
After pinning the loaded domain to V1, Knowledge Graph Overview raised
"Databricks SQL query timed out" and every KG page kept "Status
unavailable · Lakehouse". Both probes ran COUNT(*) / aggregates on the
pass-through ``…_V1_graph`` VIEW (100M-row R2RML). Explorer already used
managed ``…_entity_search`` companions; a failed probe sets
``has_data=None``, which the badge treats as unknown.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaFlatStore.py
   ``table_exists`` uses ``DESCRIBE DETAIL`` (catalog, not a row scan).
   ``get_status`` uses Delta ``numRecords`` on tables, otherwise
   ``SELECT 1 … LIMIT 1`` on ``…_entity_search``. Overview methods
   delegate to ``DeltaOverviewStats``.
2. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaOverviewStats.py
   New. Aggregate / type / predicate stats from ``_props``,
   ``_entity_search``, and ``_adj_out`` when companions exist.
3. tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_status_probe.py
   Existence and status never issue ``COUNT(*)`` on the graph VIEW.
4. tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_overview_stats.py
   Overview SQL stays on companions.
5. docs/sphinx/api/app.core.graphdb.rst
   Automodule for ``DeltaOverviewStats``.
6. docs/user-guide.md
   Overview and the status badge read graph-index companions.
7. docs/backend.md
   Same contract for Overview / status probes.

