## Count Overview totals from companions; keep status off the graph VIEW
================================================================================

Context:
After the companion-stats deploy, Overview type/predicate/label cards were
correct but Total Triples and Distinct Subjects stayed 0, the empty-state
copy still showed, and the badge remained Status unavailable. SEA
``DESCRIBE DETAIL`` does not return usable ``numRecords``, and
``DESCRIBE DETAIL`` on the pass-through ``…_graph`` VIEW still failed,
so ``has_data`` stayed null.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaOverviewStats.py
   ``COUNT(*)`` on ``_props`` / ``_entity_search`` for totals and
   subjects (same path as type distribution). No ``DESCRIBE DETAIL``.
2. src/back/core/graphdb/delta/DeltaFlatStore.py
   Graph existence and status probe ``…_entity_search`` only; never
   describe or scan ``…_graph``.
3. tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_overview_stats.py
   Aggregates use ``COUNT(*)``; ``DESCRIBE DETAIL`` is forbidden.
4. tests/units/graphdb/delta/test_delta_status_probe.py
   Graph status succeeds even if ``DESCRIBE`` of the VIEW would raise.

