## Explorer right-click menus always stay inside the viewport
================================================================================

Context:
Right-clicking near the bottom (or right) of the Explorer canvas opened the
node / canvas context menu at the raw cursor position, so its lower items
were cut off by the window edge and could not be reached.

Changes:

1. src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js
   New ``_placeContextMenu(menu, x, y)``: measures the menu off-screen, flips
   it above / left of the cursor when it would cross the bottom / right edge,
   clamps it inside the viewport (8px margin), and caps ``maxHeight`` to the
   viewport height. Used by ``_showNodeContextMenu`` and ``_showContextMenu``.
2. src/front/static/query/css/query-sigmagraph.css
   ``#sgContextMenu`` / ``#sgNodeContextMenu``: ``overflow-y: auto`` so a
   capped menu scrolls (the height cap is set in JS to honour the
   root-shell-only ``100vh`` design contract).
3. tests/units/front/test_explorer_context_menu_placement.py
   Runs the helper in Node: default placement, bottom / right flip, clamp,
   viewport cap; checks both menus use it and the CSS scrolls.

